  creatureData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 27c7e9804970e6e49bdbdb028abc6734, type: 2}
  description:
  - The mass of a Wraith is almost entirely made up of dense low temperature gases.
    Any liquid or wet solid that pass through their gaseous membrane freezes within
    seconds. Fire has been shown to dispel Wraiths, but only temporarily. Additionally,
    every reported Wraith sighting has involved the presence of an almost transparent
    flower, indicating some form of correlation.
